From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:11:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the fallback ES buffer alignment check

Equality binds more tightly than bitwise AND, so the fallback alignment
macro always rejects buffers for power-of-two alignments greater than one.
Group the mask operation before comparing it with zero. This allows IOS
reload ticket queries while preserving rejection of misaligned buffers.
---
 libogc/es.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libogc/es.c b/libogc/es.c
index e9b5176..676ddb6 100644
--- a/libogc/es.c
+++ b/libogc/es.c
@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@ distribution.
 #ifdef __builtin_is_aligned
 # define ISALIGNED(x, a) __builtin_is_aligned(x, a)
 #else
-# define ISALIGNED(x, a) (((u32)x) & (a - 1) == 0)
+# define ISALIGNED(x, a) ((((u32)x) & (a - 1)) == 0)
 #endif
 
 static char __es_fs[] ATTRIBUTE_ALIGN(32) = "/dev/es";
